{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SWhkhy9kwtkoo4f6W2CX8p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline by reimplementing GNU utilities in Go from formal specs, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use cases, orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` using shared `pkg/` libraries (sys, format, testutils), differential testing harness validates output parity.\n\n**Current state:** Specifications complete through rel05.4. Code generation has run through rel05.3 in prior generations (all marked \"not started\" in code_status means code needs generating on this branch). Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) is the target.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.4 — four use cases, all spec_complete, none started:\n- rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\n- rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum\n- rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum\n- rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.4 contains four nearly identical utilities differing only in hash algorithm (crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512). All share the same CLI pattern: read files or stdin, compute checksum, print `<hash>  <filename>` lines, support `--check` mode. They fit naturally in a single implementation task within the 250-line budget, with tests as a follow-up task.\n\nNo dependencies on other incomplete releases — these utilities use only Go standard library crypto packages and the existing pkg/testutils and pkg/sys contracts.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum (rel05.4 checksum quartet)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (PRD(s) covering md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for differential testing pattern and SIGPIPE handling)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler contract)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (DiffTest and RunDiffTests contract for test file structure reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum utility using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum utility using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum utility using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum utility using crypto/sha512\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/md5sum/main.go that reads files (or stdin when no files given or file is \"-\"),\n          computes MD5 checksums via crypto/md5, and prints output in GNU coreutils format:\n          \"<hex-hash>  <filename>\" (two spaces before filename, \"-\" for stdin). Support --check mode\n          that reads a checksum file and verifies each entry, printing \"<filename>: OK\" or\n          \"<filename>: FAILED\" with a summary line and exit code 1 on any failure. Support --tag mode\n          for BSD-style output. Support --binary/-b and --text/-t flags (on POSIX systems these are\n          equivalent but affect the output marker: \" \" for text, \"*\" for binary before the filename).\n          Support --quiet, --status, and --warn flags for --check mode. Match GNU md5sum flag names\n          and short options exactly per the PRD.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/sha1sum/main.go with identical structure and flags to md5sum, substituting\n          crypto/sha1 for the hash algorithm and producing 40-character hex digests. The --tag output\n          uses \"SHA1\" as the algorithm label.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/sha256sum/main.go with identical structure and flags to md5sum, substituting\n          crypto/sha256 for the hash algorithm and producing 64-character hex digests. The --tag output\n          uses \"SHA256\" as the algorithm label.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/sha512sum/main.go with identical structure and flags to md5sum, substituting\n          crypto/sha512 for the hash algorithm and producing 128-character hex digests. The --tag output\n          uses \"SHA512\" as the algorithm label.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          All four utilities share the same CLI logic and differ only in the hash.Hash constructor\n          and algorithm label string. Factor the shared checksum logic into a helper function within\n          each main.go file (do NOT create a shared pkg/ package for this -- keep each cmd/ package\n          self-contained). Duplicating ~40 lines of shared logic across four files is acceptable and\n          preferred over a premature abstraction.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per the project shared protocol.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Use only Go standard library packages (crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512,\n          encoding/hex, flag, fmt, io, os, bufio) plus pkg/sys. No external dependencies.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Parse flags using the Go standard flag package. Register long flags (--check, --tag, --binary,\n          --text, --quiet, --status, --warn, --strict) and their short aliases (-c, -b, -t, -w).\n          Print version info on --version and usage on --help, matching GNU behavior: exit 0 for\n          --help/--version, exit 1 for errors.\n      - id: D5\n        text: |\n          Error messages go to stderr and follow GNU format: \"<utility>: <filename>: <error>\".\n          Exit code is 0 on success, 1 on any checksum mismatch or I/O error.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/md5sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/md5sum/\" and produces a working binary.\n      - id: AC2\n        text: cmd/sha1sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha1sum/\" and produces a working binary.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: cmd/sha256sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha256sum/\" and produces a working binary.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: cmd/sha512sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha512sum/\" and produces a working binary.\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          Each binary, when given a file argument, prints the correct checksum in GNU format\n          \"<hex-hash>  <filename>\" to stdout and exits 0.\n      - id: AC6\n        text: |\n          Each binary, when given no arguments, reads stdin and prints \"<hex-hash>  -\" to stdout.\n      - id: AC7\n        text: |\n          Each binary supports --check mode: reads a checksum file, verifies each entry, prints\n          OK/FAILED per line, and exits 1 if any entry fails.\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"golangci-lint run ./cmd/md5sum/ ./cmd/sha1sum/ ./cmd/sha256sum/ ./cmd/sha512sum/ passes with no errors.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27606,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27606},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db4f0b17-e64a-4187-b096-349ebd7ac2fb","uuid":"f8acdfe8-b734-4185-acc3-1b9bed0890b4"}
